Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: enable explicitly loaded TB522FU UFS probe

The initramfs contains no modules and does not auto-mount filesystems.
Load only the verified UFS modules after the USB recovery path is armed;
protect every discovered block device before reading partition tables.
Do not attach to the disabled inline-encryption provider.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
@@ -506,3 +506,14 @@
 	power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MMCX>;
 	required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_nom_l1>;
 };
+
+/* Staged read-only UFS probe: both drivers stay modular and are loaded
+ * explicitly from initramfs after USB and the return timer are verified.
+ * Stock wiring/rails above match the captured board FDT. Inline encryption
+ * is out of scope; do not depend on the disabled ICE device.
+ */
+&ufs_mem_hc {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,ice;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+&ufs_mem_phy { status = "okay"; };
